                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course introduces undergraduate clinical pharmacy students to the fundamentals of pharmacoepidemiology, including study design, data sources, bias control, real-world research, drug safety evaluation, drug utilization research, pharmacoeconomic evaluation, and critical reading of the literature. The course is practice-oriented and aims to help students interpret research findings, assess evidence quality, and support rational medication use.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
